<title>NETHERLANDS: Burma joins UN Common Fund for Commodities.</title>
<headline>Burma joins UN Common Fund for Commodities.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Burma has joined the United Nations Common Fund for Commodities as the group's 105th member, the Amsterdam-based organisation said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The Fund is an intergovernmental financial institution established under the aegis of the U.N. Conference on Trade and Development (UNCTAD) in 1980 to finance commodity research and development projects.</p>
<p>The group said Burma would benefit from membership as it now became eligible for Fund financed projects.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
